      "slug": "the-kentuckian-painting",
      "title": "The Kentuckian (painting)",
      "year": 1954,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/Benton_The_Kentuckian.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 237,
      "imageHeight": 300,
      "story": "The Kentuckian is a 1954 painting by American artist Thomas Hart Benton. It is based on a scene from the film The Kentuckian, where the backwoodsman Big Eli Wakefield and his son Little Eli encounter a frontier village. The painting belongs to the Los Angeles County Museum of Art.",
      "facts": [
        "The painting was commissioned by the film studio Norma Productions to help promote the film The Kentuckian, directed by and starring Burt Lancaster.",
        "Both Lancaster and the producer Harold Hecht were admirers of Benton and took the initiative for the commission."
